0
00:00:00,901 --> 00:00:03,270
Tyra: PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,"

1
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:05,739
AMANDA REVEALED
A SHOCKING SECRET.

2
00:00:05,739 --> 00:00:06,840
Amanda: I'M LEGALLY BLIND.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:07,574
(gasps)

4
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:09,843
Amanda: AND I'M GONNA BE
ABOUT 30 WHEN I GO

5
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:11,345
COMPLETELY BLIND.

6
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,714
Tyra: DRAMATIC MAKEOVERS
LED TO FIERCE NEW LOOKS

7
00:00:13,714 --> 00:00:15,682
AND BOLDER PERSONALITIES.

8
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:17,851
WHEN JULIE TOLD THE JUDGES
SHE'D RATHER BE A FASHION

9
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:21,355
MERCHANDISER THAN A MODEL,
SHE WAS SENT HOME.

10
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:22,589
11 GIRLS REMAIN.

11
00:00:22,589 --> 00:00:24,992
WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

12
00:00:24,992 --> 00:00:28,195
♪♪♪

13
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:10,270
(alarm clock beeping)

14
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:12,773
Kelle: I'D BEEN SO CONFIDENT

15
00:01:12,773 --> 00:01:15,375
THROUGH THIS WHOLE THING,
BUT MY LAST PANEL--

16
00:01:15,375 --> 00:01:16,944
GOD, THAT WAS HARD.

17
00:01:16,944 --> 00:01:18,845
MY BIGGEST CHALLENGE
IS REALIZING THAT,

18
00:01:18,845 --> 00:01:21,181
HEY, YOU DON'T KNOW IT ALL.

19
00:01:21,181 --> 00:01:23,016
Kristi: I AM THE LEAST
CONFIDENT,

20
00:01:23,016 --> 00:01:25,352
AND I FEEL A LITTLE...

21
00:01:25,352 --> 00:01:27,554
INTIMIDATED OF THE OTHER GIRLS.

22
00:01:27,554 --> 00:01:30,924
I HAVE A LONG WAY TO GO,
AND THEY KNOW THAT.

23
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:33,860
Jennipher: BEING IN NEW YORK
IS TOTALLY DIFFERENT

24
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:34,928
THAN BEING IN IDAHO.

25
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:36,897
THERE'S LOTS OF DRAMA THAT
GOES ON IN THIS COMPETITION.

26
00:01:36,897 --> 00:01:39,132
cBUT I STILL LIKE EVERYBODY
IN THE HOUSE.

27
00:01:39,132 --> 00:01:41,234
AND YOU HAVE TO GET ALONG
TO LIVE TOGETHER.

28
00:01:41,234 --> 00:01:42,769
Norelle: COME ON, COME ON.

29
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:44,438
COME ON, COME ON, COME ON.

30
00:01:45,672 --> 00:01:47,841
Kristi: YOU GUYS,
WE GOT TYRA MAIL.

31
00:01:47,841 --> 00:01:48,742
I'M GONNA READ IT.

32
00:01:48,742 --> 00:01:50,677
"SCHOOL IS IN SESSION THIS A.M.

33
00:01:50,677 --> 00:01:53,914
GRAB YOUR SWEATS AND SNEAKERS
AND HEAD FOR THE GYM."

34
00:01:53,914 --> 00:01:55,282
SO WE HAVE FIVE MINUTES.

35
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:00,654
Eva: OH, WOW.

36
00:02:00,654 --> 00:02:01,688
Jennipher: SO WE SHOW UP.

37
00:02:01,688 --> 00:02:03,290
WE COME IN
AND IT'S LIKE A THEATER ROOM

38
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:05,425
AND THERE'S A STAGE
AND A RUNWAY SET UP.

39
00:02:05,425 --> 00:02:06,727
AND WE'RE LIKE,
"OH, THIS IS AWESOME.

40
00:02:06,727 --> 00:02:09,229
WE'RE GONNA DO RUNWAY TODAY."

41
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:12,032
Women: (gasping)
(applauding)

42
00:02:17,938 --> 00:02:19,172
Toccara: MISS J. COMES DOWN.

43
00:02:19,172 --> 00:02:22,009
SHE HAS HER LITTLE APPLE,
AND SHE'S JUST FABULOUS.

44
00:02:22,009 --> 00:02:23,744
Jennipher: J. ALEXANDER
IS PROBABLY THE FUNNIEST MAN

45
00:02:23,744 --> 00:02:25,545
I'VE EVER SEEN.

46
00:02:25,545 --> 00:02:28,615
Kristi: OKAY, WHY DOESN'T
SOMEONE EXPLAIN J. TO US?

47
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:32,586
HE WEARS HEELS, AND NO ONE SAYS
ANYTHING ABOUT IT.

48
00:02:32,586 --> 00:02:36,423
J.: SO, LADIES,
WELCOME TO RUNWAY 101.

49
00:02:36,423 --> 00:02:38,158
CALL ME MISS J.

50
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:40,761
REMEMBER,
AT THE J. RUNWAY SCHOOL--

51
00:02:40,761 --> 00:02:42,429
PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT.

52
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:45,132
AND A PERFECT EXAMPLE
OF THAT IS...

53
00:02:45,132 --> 00:02:47,834
MISS AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL
HERSELF--

54
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:48,502
Eva: AAH!

55
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:50,404
(cheers and applause)

56
00:02:58,679 --> 00:03:02,416
Amanda: MISS YOANNA
WALKS ON DOWN, AND IT'S PRETTY

57
00:03:02,416 --> 00:03:05,485
ENTHRALLING TO SEE SOMEBODY
THAT HAS THE EXPERIENCE.

58
00:03:05,485 --> 00:03:06,520
Yoanna: HI, HOW ARE YOU?

59
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,320
Women: HI!

60
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,288
Woman: SO HOW'S IT GOING?

61
00:03:08,288 --> 00:03:09,556
Yoanna: IT'S GOING
REALLY WELL.

62
00:03:09,556 --> 00:03:13,393
MY LIFE HAS JUST TOTALLY BEEN
FLIPPED AROUND INSIDE AND OUT,

63
00:03:13,393 --> 00:03:14,561
AND JUST BE PREPARED.

64
00:03:14,561 --> 00:03:15,696
Kristi: SO
WHILE YOU WERE HERE,

65
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:17,397
DO YOU REMEMBER FEELING
DISCOURAGED?

66
00:03:17,397 --> 00:03:20,000
JUST BECAUSE IT'S HARD TO LIKE,
CONTINUE TO BE CONFIDENT?

67
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,535
Yoanna: I THINK AS FAR AS
CONFIDENCE,

68
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:23,437
MY PHILOSOPHY IS DON'T LOOK
AT THE OTHER PERSON,

69
00:03:23,437 --> 00:03:25,172
WHAT THEY'RE DOING,
IT'S WHAT YOU'RE DOING.

70
00:03:25,172 --> 00:03:27,040
IT'S WHAT YOU CAN DO
FOR YOURSELF.

71
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,542
'CAUSE I THINK IF YOU REALLY
START WORRYING ABOUT

72
00:03:28,542 --> 00:03:31,044
THE OTHER GIRLS,
THAT YOU LOSE FOCUS.

73
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:32,846
YOU LOSE YOUR CONCENTRATION
AND THAT'S THE KEY.

74
00:03:32,846 --> 00:03:34,548
SO I KNOW WHAT YOU GUYS
ARE GOING THROUGH,

75
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:35,415
BUT IT'S WORTH IT.

76
00:03:35,415 --> 00:03:37,150
IT'S SUCH A SHORT TIME,
AND YOU'RE SO YOUNG,

77
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:39,786
AND YOU'LL SLEEP WHEN
YOU'RE DEAD SO...

78
00:03:41,288 --> 00:03:42,889
Nicole: YOANNA--SHE'S SAYING,
YOU KNOW,

79
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,191
STAY FOCUSED ON YOURSELF.

80
00:03:44,191 --> 00:03:46,326
DON'T WORRY ABOUT
WHAT THE OTHER GIRLS ARE DOING.

81
00:03:46,326 --> 00:03:48,295
AND I THINK
THAT'S REALLY SOUND ADVICE.

82
00:03:48,295 --> 00:03:50,330
Amanda: ALL RIGHT, YAY!

83
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:52,265
Yoanna: MEETING THE GIRLS,
IT'S REALLY INTERESTING

84
00:03:52,265 --> 00:03:53,533
BEING ON THE OTHER SIDE.

85
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:55,802
J. IS GONNA RESHAPE AND MOLD
THESE GIRLS TODAY,

86
00:03:55,802 --> 00:03:58,572
AND HE'S GONNA GIVE THEM
THE TOOLS TO SUCCEED.

87
00:03:58,572 --> 00:04:02,743
J.: OKAY, GIRLS,
I NEED TO SEE LEGS.

88
00:04:02,743 --> 00:04:03,877
Women: WHOO!

89
00:04:03,877 --> 00:04:05,712
J.: FIND YOUR SIZE.

90
00:04:05,712 --> 00:04:10,217
AND IF IT'S NOT YOUR SIZE,
MAKE IT WORK. MAKE IT HAPPEN.

91
00:04:10,217 --> 00:04:13,286
Amanda: OKAY, SERIOUSLY,
WHERE'S THE 8 IN THIS?

92
00:04:13,286 --> 00:04:15,889
Norelle: I AM NOT USED TO
WEARING, LIKE, HIGH HEELS.

93
00:04:15,889 --> 00:04:17,457
WHICH--I'M WORKING
ON WEARING HIGH HEELS

94
00:04:17,457 --> 00:04:18,825
BUT NOT TO THIS EXTREME.

95
00:04:18,825 --> 00:04:21,762
J.: YOU ARE NOW
IN THE "J. WALKING SCHOOL"--

96
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:24,097
WHERE POSTURE IS EVERYTHING.

97
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,298
OKAY, BABY, HIT IT.

98
00:04:25,298 --> 00:04:28,969
BOOKS ARE GONNA HELP THE GIRLS
WITH THEIR BALANCE FOR POSTURE.

99
00:04:28,969 --> 00:04:31,271
Yaya: (gasps)
J.: BALANCE IS EVERYTHING!

100
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:34,174
POSTURE, BALANCE,
POSTURE, BALANCE.

101
00:04:34,174 --> 00:04:36,676
MISS T., HONEY, YOU--YOU--

102
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:40,947
J.: (imitates buzzer)
MAKE IT WORK.

103
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,349
NOW FORGET THE BOOK ON THE HEAD.

104
00:04:42,349 --> 00:04:44,484
Jennipher: AH!

105
00:04:44,484 --> 00:04:45,819
J.: Y'ALL ARE SO BEAT UP.

106
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:52,993
J.: OKAY, OKAY,
YOU GAVE A LITTLE BIT EXTRA.

107
00:04:52,993 --> 00:04:54,761
Ann: AND THAT, LADIES,
IS HOW IT'S DONE.

108
00:04:55,896 --> 00:04:57,264
J.: YOU WALK LIKE
YOU'RE CHEWING GUM

109
00:04:57,264 --> 00:04:58,632
BETWEEN YOUR LEGS.
I LOVE IT.

110
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,867
Eva: THE GIRLS DON'T KNOW
THAT I STRUGGLE WITH THE FACT

111
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:02,669
THAT I'M THE SHORTEST GIRL
IN THE HOUSE.

112
00:05:02,669 --> 00:05:05,305
I FEEL LIKE THE TALLEST GIRL,
AND I ACT LIKE THE TALLEST GIRL.

113
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:07,274
J.: IT'S REALLY FUNNY,
BECAUSE IT'S ABOUT TO FALL,

114
00:05:07,274 --> 00:05:08,408
BUT YOU'RE NOT
LETTING IT HAPPEN.

115
00:05:08,408 --> 00:05:09,709
Eva: IT'S NOT GONNA FALL.

116
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:11,244
J.: OH! OH!

117
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:16,383
KELLE--SHE NEEDS TO BE LOOSE,
TO BE LESS...

118
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:21,855
NICOLE--SHE IS AFRAID
TO REALLY LET GO.

119
00:05:21,855 --> 00:05:23,690
CASSIE--I THINK SHE CAN DO
A LOT BETTER,

120
00:05:23,690 --> 00:05:24,691
BUT SHE'S HOLDING BACK.

121
00:05:24,691 --> 00:05:26,193
IT'S HELPFUL.
IT GIVES YOU SOME HEIGHT.

122
00:05:26,193 --> 00:05:28,562
AND AMANDA--SHE STANDS OUT.
IT'S HER EYES.

123
00:05:28,562 --> 00:05:30,130
THAT'S ALL SHE NEEDS--
THOSE EYES.

124
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:33,133
Amanda: I HAVE
A DEGENERATIVE DISEASE--

125
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:34,401
RETINITIS PIGMENTOSA.

126
00:05:34,401 --> 00:05:36,937
AND EVENTUALLY
I WILL BE COMPLETELY BLIND.

127
00:05:36,937 --> 00:05:39,673
MODELING WILL PROMOTE
CERTAIN CHALLENGES.

128
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:43,176
I'M NOT GONNA LET IT AFFECT ME
BECAUSE I DON'T WANT IT TO.

129
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:47,047
J.: WHAT I THINK WE'RE
LACKING IS GRACE AND ELEGANCE.

130
00:05:50,217 --> 00:05:53,153
J.: JENNIPHER, I DON'T FEEL
AN OUNCE OF GRACE

131
00:05:53,153 --> 00:05:54,287
IN ANY OF THOSE BONES.

132
00:05:54,287 --> 00:05:55,488
THERE'S NO LIGHTNESS TO HER.

133
00:05:55,488 --> 00:05:57,023
IT'S ALMOST...

134
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:03,563
MISS TOCCARA,
WE KNOW YOU'RE PLUS-SIZED.

135
00:06:03,563 --> 00:06:04,464
SUCK THE GUT, BABY.

136
00:06:04,464 --> 00:06:07,033
ANYTHING HANGING OUT,
IT LOOKS NASTY.

137
00:06:08,802 --> 00:06:10,770
J.: KRISTI--
I THINK THAT HER LOOK

138
00:06:10,770 --> 00:06:12,672
IS QUITE DEAD.
SHE NEEDS TO COME ALIVE.

139
00:06:12,672 --> 00:06:13,773
SHE NEEDS TO SMILE
WITH HER FACE.

140
00:06:13,773 --> 00:06:17,677
YOU ARE SERVING A PLATE OF STEAM
IN A BOWL OF NOTHING.

141
00:06:17,677 --> 00:06:19,279
Kristi: I KNOW
I WASN'T VERY GOOD.

142
00:06:19,279 --> 00:06:20,881
IT'S JUST BECAUSE
I WAS THINKING SO MUCH.

143
00:06:22,182 --> 00:06:24,084
J.: THERE'S A LOT OF...

144
00:06:24,084 --> 00:06:27,187
YAYA--
SHE'S TOO MUCH OF A DANCER.

145
00:06:27,187 --> 00:06:28,421
TRY NOT TO DO THIS.

146
00:06:29,522 --> 00:06:32,225
NORELLE IS CONCENTRATING
TOO MUCH ON THE CLOTHING

147
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,560
THAN HER BODY ITSELF.

148
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:36,329
Norelle: I WAS SERIOUSLY
THE WORST GIRL WALKING,

149
00:06:36,329 --> 00:06:37,464
AND, LIKE, FALLING.

150
00:06:37,464 --> 00:06:39,032
THIS IS SOMETHING I WOULD DO.

151
00:06:39,032 --> 00:06:41,268
BUT I'M NOT GONNA
LOOK LIKE A DUMB, LIKE, IDIOT.

152
00:06:41,268 --> 00:06:43,536
J.: SO GO AHEAD.

153
00:06:43,536 --> 00:06:46,539
Jennipher: J. MADE US WEAR
THESE HUGE HEADDRESSES,

154
00:06:46,539 --> 00:06:50,176
AND THEY WERE THE MOST AWFULEST
THINGS TO WEAR IN THE WORLD.

155
00:06:50,176 --> 00:06:51,745
J.: THE LAST FALL
WINTER COUTURE SHOW

156
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:53,947
FOR CHRISTIAN DIOR,
THERE WAS A LOT OF HEADDRESSES

157
00:06:53,947 --> 00:06:55,282
INVOLVED IN THE SHOW.

158
00:06:55,282 --> 00:06:57,083
YOU REALLY HAD A LOT
OF WORK TO DO.

159
00:06:57,083 --> 00:06:58,251
THERE IS NO REHEARSAL.

160
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,420
Norelle: WHOA.

161
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,289
Eva: (laughs)
J.: OKAY.

162
00:07:02,289 --> 00:07:03,957
(claps twice)
RIGHT HERE, LISTEN.

163
00:07:03,957 --> 00:07:06,593
EVERYTHING THAT I TAUGHT YOU,
YOU WILL BE TESTED ON IT

164
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:09,596
BECAUSE REMEMBER,
THIS IS A COMPETITION.

165
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:12,399
AND FOR BEING SUCH GOOD SPORTS,
I'M TAKING YOU OUT

166
00:07:12,399 --> 00:07:13,566
TO A PRIVATE PARTY TONIGHT.

167
00:07:13,566 --> 00:07:15,001
Women: YAY!

168
00:07:15,001 --> 00:07:17,971
J.: IT'S JUST SIMPLE
MODELS OUT ON THE TOWN

169
00:07:17,971 --> 00:07:22,242
HAVING A FIERCE TIME, OKAY?

170
00:07:22,242 --> 00:07:23,643
Women: ALL RIGHT! YAY!

171
00:07:26,947 --> 00:07:28,782
Jennipher: WE GET TO A CLUB--
LIKE A DANCE CLUB,

172
00:07:28,782 --> 00:07:30,183
AND PEOPLE WERE WAITING
OUT FRONT.

173
00:07:30,183 --> 00:07:32,018
AND WE'RE LIKE,
"HUH, THIS IS WEIRD."

174
00:07:32,018 --> 00:07:34,788
J.: RIGHT UP THIS WAY, GIRLS.

175
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:37,023
Norelle: WE WALK INTO
THIS ROOM AND THEN, YOU KNOW,

176
00:07:37,023 --> 00:07:38,224
I JUST TURNED MY HEAD.

177
00:07:38,224 --> 00:07:40,560
Women: (screaming)
Norelle: MY FAVORITE

178
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:44,397
DESIGNERS IN THE WHOLE WORLD--
HEATHERETTE IS STANDING

179
00:07:44,397 --> 00:07:46,199
RIGHT IN FRONT OF ME.

180
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:47,968
J.: I WANT YOU GUYS
TO MEET MY FRIENDS.

181
00:07:47,968 --> 00:07:48,868
Norelle: THEY'RE MY FRIENDS!

182
00:07:48,868 --> 00:07:50,737
J.: RICHIE RICH,
TRAVER RAINS,

183
00:07:50,737 --> 00:07:52,806
FROM THE HOUSE OF HEATHERETTE.

184
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:54,207
WORK IT OUT!

185
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:56,476
SO, GUYS, TELL THE GIRLS,
AND TELL US, I MEAN,

186
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:57,744
SOME OF THE PEOPLE
THAT YOU'VE DRESSED.

187
00:07:57,744 --> 00:07:59,079
SOME OF THE MOST FABULOUS
AND INCREDIBLE PEOPLE

188
00:07:59,079 --> 00:07:59,913
THAT YOU'VE WORKED WITH.

189
00:07:59,913 --> 00:08:01,281
Richie: SARAH JESSICA PARKER,
PARIS HILTON.

190
00:08:01,281 --> 00:08:03,483
Norelle: I LOVE THE WAY
PARIS HILTON DRESSES,

191
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,784
AND I LOVE PARIS HILTON.

192
00:08:04,784 --> 00:08:06,319
Richie: GWEN STEFANI,
AEROSMITH, NICOLE KIDMAN.

193
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,387
Eva: OH.

194
00:08:07,387 --> 00:08:09,756
Richie: COURTNEY LOVE.

195
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:11,424
J.: HOLD SOME OF THESE NAMES
THEY'VE BEEN DROPPING.

196
00:08:11,424 --> 00:08:13,126
Richie: LOTS OF GORGEOUS
MODELS.

197
00:08:13,126 --> 00:08:15,428
J.: THEIR SHOW IS USUALLY
THE HOTTEST TICKET IN TOWN

198
00:08:15,428 --> 00:08:16,629
DURING NEW YORK FASHION WEEK.

199
00:08:16,629 --> 00:08:18,298
IT'S SO HOT THAT I DON'T
GET A TICKET.

200
00:08:18,298 --> 00:08:21,668
(imitates sizzling noise)
THAT'S OKAY.

201
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:23,269
BUT GUESS WHAT, GIRLS.

202
00:08:23,269 --> 00:08:25,171
YOU ARE STARRING IN IT LIVE!

203
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:27,474
Women: (screaming)
OH, MY GOD!

204
00:08:27,474 --> 00:08:30,844
J.: OKAY, HAIR AND MAKEUP--
YOUR TEAM AWAITS YOU THERE.

205
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:33,413
GO FOR IT!

206
00:08:33,413 --> 00:08:34,914
Richie: THE THEME OF THIS
SHOW IS "THE CIRCUS OF PANIC"

207
00:08:34,914 --> 00:08:35,782
SO...

208
00:08:35,782 --> 00:08:36,482
Traver: (chuckles)
Richie: WITHOUT A LITTLE BIT

209
00:08:36,482 --> 00:08:38,251
OF PANICKING, AND LIKE,
ENTHUSIASM, IT WOULDN'T

210
00:08:38,251 --> 00:08:39,986
CONVEY ANYTHING ON THE RUNWAY.

211
00:08:39,986 --> 00:08:43,423
Toccara: (laughs)
Amanda: I AM SO STOKED.

212
00:08:43,423 --> 00:08:46,159
AS LONG AS I SEE THE RUNWAY
BEFORE, I'LL BE COOL.

213
00:08:47,227 --> 00:08:48,428
Norelle: WHAT?!

214
00:08:49,729 --> 00:08:51,197
HOLY CRAP.

215
00:08:54,401 --> 00:08:55,602
Nicole: OKAY.

216
00:08:55,602 --> 00:08:56,970
Danilo: OKAY, GO TO MAKEUP
TO FINISH YOU OFF.

217
00:08:56,970 --> 00:08:57,971
Cassie: OKAY.

218
00:09:04,778 --> 00:09:05,678
Richie: I'M EXCITED.

219
00:09:05,678 --> 00:09:06,546
Traver: THEY'RE GONNA
ROCK IT.

220
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:07,514
Richie: DO WE HAVE TO WALK
ON THAT RUNWAY?

221
00:09:07,514 --> 00:09:09,482
IT'S LIKE THIS...

222
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:12,685
Amanda: COULD I TAKE A PEEK
AT THE RUNWAY?

223
00:09:14,754 --> 00:09:15,755
Amanda: I DON'T THINK
I'M GONNA GET A CHANCE

224
00:09:15,755 --> 00:09:16,923
TO SEE IT BEFOREHAND.

225
00:09:16,923 --> 00:09:18,625
SO, UH, THAT KINDA SUCKS.

226
00:09:18,625 --> 00:09:20,393
I'M LEGALLY BLIND DURING
THE DAYTIME,

227
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:21,995
AND AT NIGHT IT'S...

228
00:09:21,995 --> 00:09:23,363
COMPLETELY BLIND.

229
00:09:23,363 --> 00:09:25,265
Norelle: I SAW THE SHOES
WERE, LIKE, SO BIG.

230
00:09:25,265 --> 00:09:27,033
WE DIDN'T GET TO SEE
THE RUNWAY AT ALL.

231
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:28,101
AND THESE SHOES WERE RIDICULOUS.

232
00:09:28,101 --> 00:09:29,302
I WAS LIKE, "OH, MY GOD."

233
00:09:30,804 --> 00:09:32,572
Amanda: I MEAN, I UNDERSTAND
THEY DIDN'T WANT ME TO HAVE

234
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,507
AN UNFAIR ADVANTAGE.

235
00:09:34,507 --> 00:09:37,210
BUT I'M JUST TRYING TO GET UP
TO THE SAME PLAYING FIELD

236
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:38,244
AS EVERYBODY ELSE.

237
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:39,245
Man: EVA!

238
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:41,047
Eva: OKAY, EVA'S COMING!

239
00:09:41,047 --> 00:09:42,649
Man: I NEED CASSIE.

240
00:09:42,649 --> 00:09:43,516
Man #2: GOTTA GO LINE UP.

241
00:09:43,516 --> 00:09:45,552
Cassie: I'LL GO.
Man: I NEED AMANDA.

242
00:09:45,552 --> 00:09:46,753
Amanda: I'M GETTING
SCARED NOW.

243
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:48,288
I DON'T WANNA FALL OFF
THE RUNWAY.

244
00:09:48,288 --> 00:09:50,390
J.: REMEMBER,
THIS IS A CHALLENGE,

245
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:53,560
AND EVERYTHING YOU DO
FROM THIS POINT ON,

246
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,228
YOU'RE GOING TO BE JUDGED ON.

247
00:10:06,506 --> 00:10:07,774
Woman: OKAY,
YOU GUYS, LINE UP.

248
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:09,342
Cassie: AND EVERYONE
WAS, LIKE, SO EXCITED

249
00:10:09,342 --> 00:10:12,145
BECAUSE WE WERE DOING
A FASHION SHOW FOR HEATHERETTE,

250
00:10:12,145 --> 00:10:13,947
AND IT WAS A CHALLENGE.

251
00:10:13,947 --> 00:10:16,883
J.: GIRLS, AT THE END
OF THE RUNWAY

252
00:10:16,883 --> 00:10:21,454
YOU HAVE TO STEP UP
ON THE ROUND, CIRCULAR STAGE,

253
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:23,156
POSE AND WALK AROUND IT.

254
00:10:23,156 --> 00:10:25,125
Amanda: HAVING REALLY BAD
DAYTIME VISION

255
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:28,328
AND THEN, AT NIGHT,
I'M BASICALLY COMPLETELY BLIND,

256
00:10:28,328 --> 00:10:30,530
IT WAS REALLY, REALLY SCARY.

257
00:10:30,530 --> 00:10:32,398
Man: JENNIPHER, NOW!

258
00:10:32,398 --> 00:10:33,500
Jennipher: I WAS SO NERVOUS.

259
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:35,268
"ALL RIGHT, EVERYBODY GET READY,
YOU KNOW, WE GOTTA GO.

260
00:10:35,268 --> 00:10:36,536
YOU'RE FIRST UP."

261
00:10:39,272 --> 00:10:41,808
Audience: (cheers)

262
00:10:44,277 --> 00:10:45,712
Man: LET'S GO, EVA.

263
00:10:45,712 --> 00:10:49,349
(cheers and applause)

264
00:10:49,349 --> 00:10:51,084
Eva: I WAS SO HIGH
BEING ONSTAGE.

265
00:10:51,084 --> 00:10:53,153
THOUGH I'M SHORT,
I LOVE RUNWAY.

266
00:10:53,153 --> 00:10:55,188
IT'S SO FLY TO ME.

267
00:10:55,188 --> 00:10:56,689
Man: I NEED CASSIE.

268
00:10:56,689 --> 00:10:57,891
GO.

269
00:11:02,896 --> 00:11:05,298
Man: I NEED ANN. GO, GO, GO.

270
00:11:08,568 --> 00:11:09,769
J.: LET'S GO, KELLE.

271
00:11:11,437 --> 00:11:13,039
Man: I NEED NICOLE.

272
00:11:15,909 --> 00:11:17,110
TOCCARA.

273
00:11:18,077 --> 00:11:20,346
(cheers and applause)

274
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:22,315
Toccara: I LOVE THE CROWD.
I LOVE TO HEAR EVERYONE CHEER.

275
00:11:22,315 --> 00:11:23,716
I LOVE TO BE THE SPOTLIGHT.

276
00:11:23,716 --> 00:11:25,251
I LIKE TO BE THE CENTER
OF ATTENTION.

277
00:11:25,251 --> 00:11:27,487
I LOVE TO BE A SHOWSTOPPER
SO I LOVED IT.

278
00:11:27,487 --> 00:11:29,289
Eva: TOCCARA ACTUALLY
DISCLOSED THIS TO ME,

279
00:11:29,289 --> 00:11:31,324
THAT SHE THOUGHT SHE WAS GONNA
WIN BECAUSE SHE GOT A LOT

280
00:11:31,324 --> 00:11:32,725
OF APPLAUSE.

281
00:11:32,725 --> 00:11:35,328
YOU GOT APPLAUSE
BECAUSE YOUR... WERE OUT, GIRL.

282
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:38,298
Man: WHERE'S YAYA?

283
00:11:38,298 --> 00:11:39,566
GO.

284
00:11:46,339 --> 00:11:47,307
Richie: GOOD!

285
00:11:47,307 --> 00:11:47,974
Man: I NEED KRISTI.

286
00:11:47,974 --> 00:11:49,008
Kristi: WHOO!

287
00:11:49,008 --> 00:11:50,543
THERE WERE LOTS OF GUYS
STANDING DOWN THERE,

288
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:52,345
AND I WAS LIKE, "YOU CAN TOTALLY
SEE UP MY SKIRT.

289
00:11:52,345 --> 00:11:53,379
I KNOW YOU CAN."

290
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:55,348
AND YOU GET HIGHER
WHEN YOU GET UP ON THE CIRCLE.

291
00:11:55,348 --> 00:11:56,983
I WAS JUST LIKE,
"GET ME OFF THIS CIRCLE.

292
00:11:56,983 --> 00:11:58,418
GET ME DOWN AWAY FROM HERE."

293
00:11:58,418 --> 00:11:59,852
Richie: NOBODY'S FALLEN DOWN
YET, RIGHT?

294
00:11:59,852 --> 00:12:01,521
Man: I NEED AMANDA.

295
00:12:03,656 --> 00:12:05,758
Amanda: I COULDN'T SEE
THE RUNWAY.

296
00:12:05,758 --> 00:12:08,328
PEOPLE WOULDN'T EVEN TELL ME
THE NUMBER OF STEPS LEADING UP

297
00:12:08,328 --> 00:12:09,462
TO THE RUNWAY.

298
00:12:09,462 --> 00:12:10,997
I WAS REALLY SURPRISED.

299
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:15,568
AS SOON AS I HIT THAT FIRST STEP
I SAW THAT THE RUNWAY

300
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:16,703
HAD GLITTER ALL OVER IT.

301
00:12:16,703 --> 00:12:19,772
I WAS LIKE, "THANK YOU!"
'CAUSE THE GLITTER SAVED ME.

302
00:12:29,549 --> 00:12:32,252
Norelle: IT FEELS SO GOOD
THAT I GOT TO BE IN THE SHOW.

303
00:12:32,252 --> 00:12:33,853
I MEAN,
IT'S LIKE A DREAM COME TRUE.

304
00:12:33,853 --> 00:12:35,488
FOR THE REST OF MY LIFE
I'M NEVER GONNA GET OVER IT.

305
00:12:35,488 --> 00:12:36,756
Man: GO, NORELLE.

306
00:12:43,763 --> 00:12:45,999
(record needle scratches)
Man: SHE JUST FELL DOWN.

307
00:12:48,701 --> 00:12:49,802
Richie: OH, MY GOD!

308
00:12:49,802 --> 00:12:51,938
Norelle: MY BIGGEST DREAM--
HEATHERETTE FASHION SHOW.

309
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:53,373
MY WORST NIGHTMARE--FALLING.

310
00:12:53,373 --> 00:12:54,907
ALL IN THE SAME NIGHT.

311
00:12:54,907 --> 00:12:56,743
Richie: THAT'S GONNA
MAKE YOU A STAR, BABY.

312
00:13:00,046 --> 00:13:01,714
J.: THE GIRLS ARE PSYCHED.

313
00:13:01,714 --> 00:13:05,118
THEY TOOK THEIR FIRST SHOT
OF FASHION CRACK.

314
00:13:05,118 --> 00:13:06,252
Amanda: WALKING IN
WAS FIERCE.

315
00:13:06,252 --> 00:13:08,154
AND THEN LIKE, "BOOM,"
45 MINUTES LATER

316
00:13:08,154 --> 00:13:09,255
THEY'RE LOOKING AT US.

317
00:13:09,255 --> 00:13:10,590
J.: WHERE'S YOUR STICK?

318
00:13:12,158 --> 00:13:14,394
SEE THIS IS WHAT I SHOULD'VE
HAD TODAY GIVING YOU

319
00:13:14,394 --> 00:13:15,762
THE WALKING LESSON.

320
00:13:17,664 --> 00:13:20,233
WHEN YOU'RE IN, LIKE,
A DIMLY LIT ROOM,

321
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:21,834
WHAT DO YOU SEE?

322
00:13:21,834 --> 00:13:24,337
Amanda: MY PERIPHERAL
IS SO BAD AT NIGHT.

323
00:13:24,337 --> 00:13:26,439
LIKE, I'M COMPLETELY
NIGHT-BLIND.

324
00:13:26,439 --> 00:13:29,275
AFTER THE RUNWAY WAS DONE,
I MADE A MISTAKE BY SAYING

325
00:13:29,275 --> 00:13:31,678
TO J., "YOU KNOW ABOUT MY EYES,
RIGHT?"

326
00:13:31,678 --> 00:13:33,780
Toccara: THE RUMOR IS
AMANDA'S GETTING SPECIAL

327
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:36,516
TREATMENT 'CAUSE SHE'S--
'CAUSE SHE'S... HERE.

328
00:13:36,516 --> 00:13:38,418
J.: IF MISS AMANDA DID GET
ANY KIND OF SPECIAL TREATMENT,

329
00:13:38,418 --> 00:13:38,918
I DIDN'T SEE IT.

330
00:13:38,918 --> 00:13:41,688
BECAUSE I WAS JUST TOLD
OF YOUR CONDITION.

331
00:13:41,688 --> 00:13:43,856
Amanda: I WASN'T ALLOWED
TO SEE THE RUNWAY BEFOREHAND.

332
00:13:43,856 --> 00:13:45,458
J.: I SAID NO.
NOBODY CAN SEE IT.

333
00:13:45,458 --> 00:13:46,326
SO YOU BLAME HER.

334
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:47,527
Eva: BUT IF YOU'RE GONNA
BE A MODEL,

335
00:13:47,527 --> 00:13:48,995
AND YOU'RE GONNA DO THIS,
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

336
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:50,630
Amanda: YEAH, AND I,
YOU KNOW, I DID MY THING

337
00:13:50,630 --> 00:13:51,998
OUT THERE WITHOUT SEEING IT,
YOU KNOW?

338
00:13:51,998 --> 00:13:53,800
Eva: I'M SHORT.
MY SHOE IS TOO LITTLE.

339
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,001
I DIDN'T COMPLAIN.

340
00:13:55,001 --> 00:13:57,937
J.: LIKE I ALWAYS SAY,
RUMORS DON'T START FROM NOTHIN'.

341
00:13:57,937 --> 00:14:00,406
THEY DON'T JUST FALL OUT
THE SKY. IT'S CREATED.

342
00:14:00,406 --> 00:14:03,042
SO I WILL BE ANNOUNCING
THE WINNER OF THIS CHALLENGE

343
00:14:03,042 --> 00:14:04,410
TOMORROW MORNING, OKAY?

344
00:14:04,410 --> 00:14:06,112
THANK YOU! HAVE A GOOD NIGHT.

345
00:14:10,817 --> 00:14:12,618
Toccara: I DON'T KNOW HOW
SHE'S TALKING ABOUT SHE BLIND

346
00:14:12,618 --> 00:14:15,021
WHEN SHE SAID SHE WAS OVER THERE
DOING THIS...

347
00:14:15,021 --> 00:14:16,856
AND DOING THIS...

348
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:19,926
IT LOOKED LIKE YOU WEREN'T
WORRIED ABOUT NOT SEEING TO ME.

349
00:14:19,926 --> 00:14:22,995
Yaya: BUT THEN IN THE ROOM,
SHE'S LIKE, "IS THIS A POLE?"

350
00:14:22,995 --> 00:14:26,199
Amanda: THE GIRLS THINK
I'M EXAGGERATING MY BLINDNESS.

351
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:28,334
THE MAIN INSTIGATOR IS EVA.

352
00:14:28,334 --> 00:14:33,005
I HAD A DREAM ABOUT HER WHERE
SHE WAS JUST, LIKE, BEING EVA.

353
00:14:33,005 --> 00:14:36,843
AND I BEAT HER... ASS
INTO THE GROUND.

354
00:14:36,843 --> 00:14:38,978
I WAS, LIKE, SLAMMING HER HEAD
AGAINST THE FLOOR.

355
00:14:38,978 --> 00:14:40,913
Jennipher: WELL, SHE ACTS
SO TOUGH, BUT SHE'S NOT.

356
00:14:40,913 --> 00:14:43,049
Amanda: NO, SHE'S NOT,
THAT'S WHY SHE'S SO LOUD

357
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:44,150
ALL THE TIME. SHE'S INSECURE.

358
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:46,285
Jennipher: I WANT SOMEONE
TO DOG HER ABOUT HER HEIGHT.

359
00:14:46,285 --> 00:14:47,687
Amanda: (laughs)

360
00:14:53,826 --> 00:14:55,495
Amanda: DO YOU KNOW WHERE
THE LAUNDRY CAME FROM,

361
00:14:55,495 --> 00:14:56,529
OR WHERE IT WENT?

362
00:14:56,529 --> 00:14:57,663
Cassie: YEAH, EVA BROUGHT IT.

363
00:14:57,663 --> 00:15:00,233
Amanda: YEAH,
AND SHE "DOESN'T KNOW."

364
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:03,536
Nicole: AMANDA WAS THINKING
THAT HER BELONGINGS

365
00:15:03,536 --> 00:15:05,071
WERE DISAPPEARING
AND THAT THERE WAS

366
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:07,573
A CERTAIN SOMEONE WHO HAD THEM.

367
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,909
Amanda: I FEEL THAT A LOT
OF PEOPLE IN THE HOUSE

368
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,577
DON'T TRUST EVA.

369
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,146
I'M MISSING $100.

370
00:15:13,146 --> 00:15:14,580
MY SHIRT'S GONE.

371
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,915
MY LAUNDRY IS GONE.

372
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:17,650
SHE'S THE ONE
THAT DISTRIBUTED IT.

373
00:15:17,650 --> 00:15:18,484
Jennipher: I'M MISSING STUFF.

374
00:15:18,484 --> 00:15:20,820
AND I CAN'T FIGURE OUT
WHAT I'M MISSING EXACTLY,

375
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:22,488
BUT SOMEBODY HAS IT.

376
00:15:24,157 --> 00:15:26,025
Amanda: ♪ I'M MISSING $100 ♪

377
00:15:26,025 --> 00:15:28,194
♪ AND MY LAUNDRY'S GONE ♪

378
00:15:28,194 --> 00:15:30,596
♪ 'CAUSE OF A CERTAIN BITCH
MMM! ♪

379
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:31,931
♪ CERTAIN BITCH ♪

380
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,266
♪ CERTAIN BITCH ♪♪

381
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:39,739
I DON'T KNOW IF I STARTED
THE INSTIGATION OF EVA,

382
00:15:39,739 --> 00:15:42,442
BUT IT SUCKS THAT
THE LOUDEST PERSON

383
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:44,744
IS ALSO THE ONE
THAT YOU CAN'T TRUST.

384
00:15:52,652 --> 00:15:54,187
Eva: WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

385
00:15:54,187 --> 00:15:55,721
Amanda: I'M LOOKING
FOR MY BAG.

386
00:15:55,721 --> 00:15:57,056
OKAY, BAIT ONE.

387
00:15:58,124 --> 00:15:59,025
BAIT TWO.

388
00:15:59,025 --> 00:16:00,493
SHE MIGHT NOT WANT IT,
'CAUSE THEY'RE UGLY.

389
00:16:00,493 --> 00:16:01,928
I'M NOT LEAVING MY CRYSTALS OUT.

390
00:16:01,928 --> 00:16:05,164
Nicole: I WASN'T NECESSARILY
IN SETTING THE TRAP,

391
00:16:05,164 --> 00:16:07,667
I JUST KINDA WAS LIKE,
"HEY, THAT'S A GOOD IDEA."

392
00:16:07,667 --> 00:16:10,670
Amanda: I'M GONNA LOSE
A LITTLE CASH, TOO.

393
00:16:10,670 --> 00:16:12,271
WHAT'S A $10 BILL
TO CATCH A BITCH?

394
00:16:12,271 --> 00:16:13,139
HMM?

395
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:14,040
BAM!

396
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:16,442
Nicole: I WROTE
"NICOLE'S SWEET ASS"

397
00:16:16,442 --> 00:16:19,245
ON THE BILL SO THAT IF SOMEONE
DID TAKE IT,

398
00:16:19,245 --> 00:16:20,613
WE WOULD KNOW WHO.

399
00:16:23,216 --> 00:16:25,451
Amanda: ♪ DETECTIVE ♪

400
00:16:25,451 --> 00:16:27,053
♪ DETECTIVE ♪♪

401
00:16:34,594 --> 00:16:36,229
(knock on door)

402
00:16:38,231 --> 00:16:39,499
Amanda: HELLO!

403
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:41,968
Cassie: J. CAME TO OUR HOUSE
TO ANNOUNCE WHO HAD WON

404
00:16:41,968 --> 00:16:43,402
THE CHALLENGE
FROM THE HEATHERETTE SHOW

405
00:16:43,402 --> 00:16:44,237
THE NIGHT BEFORE.

406
00:16:44,237 --> 00:16:47,273
J.: UM, ANYWAY,
DID YOU RECOVER FROM LAST NIGHT?

407
00:16:47,273 --> 00:16:48,474
Women: YEAH! YES!

408
00:16:48,474 --> 00:16:53,346
J.: THE WINNER HAS TO CHOOSE
RIGHT AWAY TWO PEOPLE

409
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:57,817
TO GO WITH HER
ON A YACHT.

410
00:16:57,817 --> 00:17:01,020
A PURE, ALL-DAY PAMPERING,
DARLINGS.

411
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,288
Eva: AAH!

412
00:17:03,589 --> 00:17:05,724
J.: AND YOUR HOST WILL BE
PICKING YOU UP IN ONE HOUR.

413
00:17:05,724 --> 00:17:07,326
SO WE'RE GONNA START
WITH MISS JENNIPHER.

414
00:17:07,326 --> 00:17:09,161
BE A LITTLE LIGHTER
WHEN YOU WALK.

415
00:17:09,161 --> 00:17:10,596
YOUR FEET CAN'T GUIDE YOU.

416
00:17:10,596 --> 00:17:12,131
Jennipher: J.
CRITICIZED MY WALK.

417
00:17:12,131 --> 00:17:14,233
IT'S KINDA FRUSTRATING BECAUSE
I TRY MY FIRST TIME

418
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:15,233
AND THEY'RE LIKE,
"OH, THAT SUCKS."

419
00:17:15,233 --> 00:17:18,271
J.: AMANDA, YOU'RE JUST
TRYING TO BE A LITTLE TOO SEXY.

420
00:17:18,271 --> 00:17:20,373
MISS EVA,
I WISH YOU WOULD'VE WORKED

421
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:22,608
THE CAPE JUST A LITTLE BIT MORE.

422
00:17:22,608 --> 00:17:23,742
JUST A BIT MORE.

423
00:17:23,742 --> 00:17:25,678
MISS ANN,
YOU WALK LIKE A DUDE.

424
00:17:25,678 --> 00:17:27,780
YOU'RE JUST SO DAMN PRETTY.

425
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:31,817
MISS TOCCARA,
YOU HELD YOUR OWN, BABY.

426
00:17:31,817 --> 00:17:33,920
YOU WERE MISS CROWD-PLEASER.

427
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,655
BUT AT THE SAME TIME,
I WAS AFRAID YOUR PUPPIES

428
00:17:35,655 --> 00:17:36,989
WOULD GET OUT OF THE CAGE.

429
00:17:36,989 --> 00:17:40,326
Eva: (laughs)
J.: OOH, I'M SO GLAD.

430
00:17:40,326 --> 00:17:43,329
MISS KRISTI,
YOU LOOKED DOWN A LOT.

431
00:17:43,329 --> 00:17:45,264
Kristi: MM-HMM.
I THINK I WAS LOOKING AT PEOPLE.

432
00:17:45,264 --> 00:17:48,167
J.: IT'S SO IMPORTANT
FOR YOU NOT TO DO THAT.

433
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:50,736
Kristi: I'M FEELING LIKE
I DON'T HAVE ANY CONTROL

434
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:52,572
OVER THE THINGS THAT I'M DOING.

435
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:55,408
J.: AND, MISS NORELLE,
WELL, I LOVE IT

436
00:17:55,408 --> 00:17:56,809
THAT IT WAS YOUR FAVORITE SHOW.

437
00:17:56,809 --> 00:17:58,878
AND IT'S YOUR FAVORITE
DESIGNERS.

438
00:17:58,878 --> 00:18:00,746
WE LIVE FOR THAT MOMENT.

439
00:18:00,746 --> 00:18:01,814
AND YOU FALL DOWN IN IT.

440
00:18:01,814 --> 00:18:03,349
YOU JUST TUMBLED.

441
00:18:03,349 --> 00:18:05,551
IT WAS MAJOR.

442
00:18:05,551 --> 00:18:07,720
SO THE WINNER
OF THIS COMPETITION

443
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:12,391
BECAUSE YOU NAILED IT,
AND WHEN I SAY, "NAILED IT,"

444
00:18:12,391 --> 00:18:13,559
IS MISS EVA.

445
00:18:13,559 --> 00:18:15,161
Eva: OH, YES!

446
00:18:15,161 --> 00:18:16,228
J.: YOU NAILED IT. YOU DID.

447
00:18:16,228 --> 00:18:17,763
